priority class is non namespace

the default priority class value of a pod is 0, if you want to change it, add this field globalDefault: true.

in priority class definition file, preemptionPolicy is defining that when there's a higher priority job being scheduled, would it kill the lower priority running
jobs first or being shceduled in higher priority then other jobs which are also being scheduled. the default value is PreemptlowerPriority, which would kill the 
running lower priority jobs, if change to 'never', it wouldnt kill the existing running jobs, instead it would be scheduled ealier than other lower priority jobs
which are being scheduled.

kubectl get priorityclass

matching this field:
in priority-class.yaml:
metadata:
  name: high-priority

in pod-definition.yaml:
spec:
  priorityClassNAme: high-priority

default value is 0 if not specified, if modify, nmust create a new priority class and assign the global default property to true. 
note that in this case it can only be defined in a single priority class.

to assign higher priority workload to a full pod, the default value of 'preemptionPolicy: PreemptLowerPriority' means stopping the lower ones and put higher ones in;
otherwise specify the value as preemptionPolicy: never

